[32m+[m[32m## How It Works[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe browser displays the project form and list. When a user adds, edits, or deletes a project, `public/script.js` sends an HTTP request to the Express API. The server validates the request and uses `database.js` to read or modify the SQLite database. The API returns a JSON response, and the browser updates the visible list.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Data flow:** Browser → `fetch()` → Express API → SQLite → JSON response → updated webpage.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## API Endpoints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| GET | `/api/health` | Check server health |[m
[32m+[m[32m| GET | `/api/projects` | Retrieve projects |[m
[32m+[m[32m| POST | `/api/projects` | Create a project |[m
[32m+[m[32m| PUT | `/api/projects/:id` | Update a project |[m
[32m+[m[32m| DELETE | `/api/projects/:id` | Delete a project |[m
[32m+[m
